    <string name="settings_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body_1">DLNE has no accounts, and this app collects nothing about you: no analytics, no ads, no tracking.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body_2">Your chats are stored only on this phone. When you send a message, the conversation so far travels over an encrypted connection to the DLNE service, which passes it to one of the computers people lend to DLNE to write the answer.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body_3">Those computers belong to other people, so don\'t send passwords, private details or anything secret. The service sees your network (IP) address, which it uses to limit how often each network can ask.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body_4">Lookups (weather, Wikipedia, news, web search) are made by the DLNE server, not your phone; reported answers are kept on the server for review.</string>
